    <summary>A fast, native Markdown editor: inline WYSIWYG editing that opens as quickly as a scratchpad. No WebView.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[Tachyon is a GPU-accelerated native Markdown editor, built for reading and editing text such as pasted LLM output. It starts as fast as a scratchpad and edits like Typora: one pane, inline WYSIWYG, no WebView.

## Features

- **Block swap editing:** the block under the caret shows raw Markdown; every other block shows rendered rich text. Files that are not Markdown open in plain-text mode (`Ctrl+Shift+M` toggles).
- **Fast:** after the first start, launches open in about one frame because Tachyon stays resident in the notification area. A keystroke paints within one frame, and a 5 MB paste never drops one.
- **Large files stay responsive:** a 200 MB log opens in about 400 MB of memory; files over 2 GiB are refused with a message instead of crashing.
- **Everyday editing:** find and replace, light and dark themes that follow Windows, zoom, `Ctrl+click` links, list continuation, syntax highlighting in fenced code, a command palette, Go to heading, quick open and Open recent, Copy as HTML, local images, Mermaid diagrams and math.
- **Hot exit and session restore:** quitting keeps unsaved documents and reopens every window where it was.
- **Sticky notes** with their own global hotkey.
- A Preferences panel (`Ctrl+,`) over a plain `settings.toml`.

## Command line

`tachyon notes.md` opens a file, `tachyon --paste` opens the clipboard, `tachyon --quit` ends the resident instance, `tachyon --autostart on` starts it at sign-in, and `tachyon --help` lists every option.

## Notes

- Requires Windows 10 (version 1903 or later) or Windows 11, 64-bit.
- This package installs the signed portable build from the GitHub release and adds a Start menu shortcut. Update it with `choco upgrade tachyon`; it does not update itself.
- The project also publishes a self-updating MSIX install (`Tachyon.appinstaller`). Use one or the other: if both are installed, `tachyon` in a terminal starts whichever comes first on your PATH.
- Uninstalling closes Tachyon if it is running from this package. Your settings, session and unsaved documents (under `%APPDATA%` and `%LOCALAPPDATA%`) are kept.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/DailenG/tachyon/releases/tag/v1.5.0</releaseNotes>
